 1. join returns the thread itself                       true
 2. value is the block's last expression                 2
 3. after it ends: alive? / status                       false / false
 4. Thread.current is Thread.main: outside / inside      true / false
 5. a new thread has its own native_thread_id            true
 6. a thread did x += 1 on the outer local; x is now     11
 7. Thread.new(1, 2) { |a, b| a + b }.value              3
 8. join re-raises the thread's exception                ArgumentError: boom
 9. status after an exception (nil, not false)           nil
10. status: a sleeping thread / the current thread       "sleep" / "run"
11. Thread.pass returns                                  nil
12. results through a Queue, sorted after join           [[0, 0], [1, 1], [2, 4]]
13. main ends -> other threads are killed (child stdout) "main done\n"
14. report_on_exception (default) -> child's stderr, line 1 "#<Thread:0x... -e:1 run> terminated with exception (report_on_exception is true):"
